.EVMAIL 1 "Evomail" "Evolution Mail CLI"

.SH NAME
evomail \- CLI for Evolution mail client using native EDS/Camel stack

.SH SYNOPSIS
.evomail [OPTION...] COMMAND [ARGS]
.br
.evomail accounts
.br
.evomail folders [OPTIONS...]
.br
.evomail list [OPTIONS...]
.br
.evomail search QUERY [OPTIONS...]
.br
.evomail read UID [OPTIONS...]
.br
.evomail search QUERY [OPTIONS...]
.br
.evomail export UID -o FILE
.br
.evomail delete UID...
.br
.evomail send [OPTIONS...]
.br
.evomail reply UID [OPTIONS...]
.br
.evomail forward UID [OPTIONS...]
.br
.evomail forward-as-attachment UID [OPTIONS...]
.br
.evomail move UID... --move-to FOLDER
.br
.evomail copy UID... --copy-to FOLDER
.br
.evomail config [OPTIONS...]
.br
.evomail --config-set-account EMAIL
.br
.evomail --config-set-folder FOLDER
.br
.evomail --config-wizard
.br
.evomail --version
.br
.evomail --help

.SH DESCRIPTION
evomail is a command-line interface for the GNOME Evolution mail client.
It uses Evolution's native EDS/Camel stack rather than reimplementing IMAP/SMTP,
providing native OAuth2 authentication, native folder management, and native
message handling.

.SH COMMANDS

.TP
accounts
List all Evolution mail accounts with their UIDs, backends, hosts, ports,
and SMTP transport UIDs.

.TP
folders [OPTIONS]
List folders for an account.
Options:
  --account ACCOUNT   Account email, name, UID, or UID prefix
  --folder FOLDER     Folder name or alias
  --json              Print JSON output

.TP
list [OPTIONS]
List messages in a folder (default: newest 20).
Options:
  --account ACCOUNT   Account email, name, UID, or UID prefix
  --folder FOLDER     Folder name or alias (inbox, sent, drafts, trash, junk, all)
  --limit N           Maximum messages to show (default: 20)
  --unread            List only unread messages
  --no-refresh        Do not synchronize the folder before listing
  --json              Print JSON output

.TP
search QUERY [OPTIONS]
Search a folder for messages.
Options:
  --account ACCOUNT   Account email, name, UID, or UID prefix
  --folder FOLDER     Folder name or alias
  --limit N           Maximum messages to show
  --no-refresh        Do not synchronize the folder before listing
  --json              Print JSON output

.TP
read UID [OPTIONS]
Print one message.
Options:
  --account ACCOUNT   Account email, name, UID, or UID prefix
  --folder FOLDER     Folder name or alias
  --json              Print JSON output
  --html              Show HTML part
  --save-attachments DIR   Save attachments to directory
  --mark-seen         Mark the message as seen after reading

.TP
search QUERY [OPTIONS]
Search a folder for messages.
Options:
  --account ACCOUNT   Account email, name, UID, or UID prefix
  --folder FOLDER     Folder name or alias
  --limit N           Maximum messages to show
  --no-refresh        Do not synchronize the folder before listing
  --json              Print JSON output

.TP
export UID -o FILE
Export a raw message to a file.
Options:
  --account ACCOUNT   Account email, name, UID, or UID prefix
  --folder FOLDER     Folder name or alias
  --output FILE       Save raw message to this file
  --json              Print JSON output

.TP
delete UID...
Delete and expunge messages.
Options:
  --account ACCOUNT   Account email, name, UID, or UID prefix
  --folder FOLDER     Folder name or alias
  --json              Print JSON output

.TP
send [OPTIONS]
Compose and send a message.
Options:
  --account ACCOUNT   Account email, name, UID, or UID prefix
  --to ADDRESSES      To recipients
  --cc ADDRESSES      Cc recipients
  --bcc ADDRESSES     Bcc recipients
  --subject TEXT      Subject
  --body TEXT         Message body
  --body-file FILE    Read body from file
  --edit              Compose body in $EDITOR
  --draft             Save to Drafts folder instead of sending
  --signature TEXT    Append signature text
  --signature-file FILE   Read signature from file
  --attach FILE       Attach file (repeatable)
  --dry-run           Build message and print summary without sending
  --no-save-copy      Do not append copy to Sent folder
  --json              Print JSON output
  --html              Treat body as HTML
  --help              Show help

.TP
reply UID [OPTIONS]
Reply to a message.
Options:
  --account ACCOUNT   Account email, name, UID, or UID prefix
  --folder FOLDER     Folder name or alias
  --to ADDRESSES      To recipients
  --cc ADDRESSES      Cc recipients
  --bcc ADDRESSES     Bcc recipients
  --subject TEXT      Subject
  --body TEXT         Message body
  --body-file FILE    Read body from file
  --edit              Compose body in $EDITOR
  --draft             Save to Drafts folder instead of sending
  --signature TEXT    Append signature text
  --signature-file FILE   Read signature from file
  --attach FILE       Attach file (repeatable)
  --dry-run           Build message and print summary without sending
  --no-save-copy      Do not append copy to Sent folder
  --json              Print JSON output
  --html              Treat body as HTML
  --reply-all         Reply to all recipients
  --help              Show help

.TP
forward UID [OPTIONS]
Forward a message.
Options:
  --account ACCOUNT   Account email, name, UID, or UID prefix
  --folder FOLDER     Folder name or alias
  --to ADDRESSES      To recipients
  --cc ADDRESSES      Cc recipients
  --bcc ADDRESSES     Bcc recipients
  --subject TEXT      Subject
  --body TEXT         Message body
  --body-file FILE    Read body from file
  --edit              Compose body in $EDITOR
  --draft             Save to Drafts folder instead of sending
  --signature TEXT    Append signature text
  --signature-file FILE   Read signature from file
  --attach FILE       Attach file (repeatable)
  --dry-run           Build message and print summary without sending
  --no-save-copy      Do not append copy to Sent folder
  --json              Print JSON output
  --html              Treat body as HTML
  --help              Show help

.TP
forward-as-attachment UID [OPTIONS]
Forward a message as .eml attachment.
Options:
  --account ACCOUNT   Account email, name, UID, or UID prefix
  --folder FOLDER     Folder name or alias
  --to ADDRESSES      To recipients
  --cc ADDRESSES      Cc recipients
  --bcc ADDRESSES     Bcc recipients
  --subject TEXT      Subject
  --body TEXT         Message body
  --body-file FILE    Read body from file
  --edit              Compose body in $EDITOR
  --draft             Save to Drafts folder instead of sending
  --signature TEXT    Append signature text
  --signature-file FILE   Read signature from file
  --attach FILE       Attach file (repeatable)
  --dry-run           Build message and print summary without sending
  --no-save-copy      Do not append copy to Sent folder
  --json              Print JSON output
  --html              Treat body as HTML
  --help              Show help

.TP
move UID... --move-to FOLDER
Move messages to a folder.
Options:
  --account ACCOUNT   Account email, name, UID, or UID prefix
  --folder FOLDER     Folder name or alias
  --move-to FOLDER    Destination folder
  --json              Print JSON output

.TP
copy UID... --copy-to FOLDER
Copy messages to a folder.
Options:
  --account ACCOUNT   Account email, name, UID, or UID prefix
  --folder FOLDER     Folder name or alias
  --copy-to FOLDER    Destination folder
  --json              Print JSON output

.TP
config [OPTIONS]
Configure evomail settings.
Options:
  --json              Print JSON output

.TP
--config-set-account ACCOUNT
Set default account.

.TP
--config-set-folder FOLDER
Set default folder.

.TP
--config-wizard
Interactive setup wizard.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
EVOMAIL_ACCOUNT
Selects the default account when not specified on command line.

.SH FILES
.TP
~/.config/evomail/config.ini
Configuration file with default account and folder settings.

